Staff Data Scientist, Trust & Safety &lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brief info about Vinted&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Our mission is to make second-hand the first choice, and we&#39;re looking for people who want to help us get there. Every day, we work together to help our members buy and sell pre-loved clothing and lifestyle items, giving each piece a second life – or even a third. &lt;br&gt;The Vinted Group is made up of three business units that support this mission:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/marketplace&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Vinted Marketplace&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; is Europe’s leading platform for second-hand fashion and a go-to destination for all kinds of pre-loved items, with a growing range of categories. Our platform connects millions of members across 20+ markets, helping great items find a new life.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedgo&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Go&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; enhances the shipping experience with a vast network of over 500,000 pick-up and drop-off points, partnering with more than 60 carriers across Europe, with added services like item verification for peace of mind on high-value pieces.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedpay&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Pay&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is the newest part of the Vinted Group, dedicated to bringing secure, reliable payments to buyers and sellers across Europe. Seamlessly integrated into the Vinted app, it helps keep every transaction safe, efficient, and easy for our members.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2008 in Lithuania, Vinted began as a way for friends to find new homes for clothes they no longer needed. In 2019, we became Lithuania&#39;s first unicorn! Today, our headquarters remain in Vilnius, and we&#39;ve grown with offices across Europe, supported by a team of over 2,000 people.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Information about the position&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join Vinted&#39;s Trust &amp;amp; Safety domain, whose mission is to protect the Vinted community from harmful activities and content. Across several detection, moderation and sanctioning teams, we run a growing set of machine learning models, rule engines, and LLM agents. They score every new listing, account and message at Vinted&#39;s scale, and many of them act on members automatically.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Staff Data Scientist to shape the architecture and effectiveness of our detection systems as a whole. You&#39;ll tackle problems that individual teams cannot solve independently: how to maximize detection coverage, combine different models into coherent risk decisions, and allocate computational resources where they reduce the most harm.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior individual contributor role with scope across Trust &amp;amp; Safety and Security domains. You&#39;ll set technical direction, challenge existing approaches, prototype solutions and work with teams to bring them into production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It&#39;s an opportunity to shape how a large-scale, increasingly AI-driven safety system is built, evaluated and improved.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this position, you’ll&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design the end-to-end ML architecture for detection, risk scoring, routing and decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop cost-efficient, layered inference strategies that combine broad, low-latency screening with deeper, more expensive analysis where it adds the most value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish approaches to continuous risk assessment across the member lifecycle, from registration and listing creation to ongoing activity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define how we measure end-to-end detection effectiveness, including precision, coverage, missed harm and computational cost. Use these measurements to identify the highest-impact improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn siloed, team-level models into a coherent, calibrated detection system by addressing the technical and organisational barriers that lead to local optimisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and close detection coverage gaps, ensuring that relevant signals and outcomes are available for evaluation, diagnosis and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set shared technical standards and architectural direction across teams, working with engineering and data science leaders to translate them into production systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype critical components, test architectural assumptions empirically and build reference implementations that teams can scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explain complex ML trade-offs to senior technical and business leaders as clear choices about harm reduction, cost, and engineering investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 8+ years of experience in Data Science, Machine Learning, or a similar role, including significant time owning production models or model evaluation at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have led cross-team technical work without formal authority, and you&#39;re comfortable setting standards that other teams adopt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have deep expertise in statistical inference and experimentation: A/B testing, measuring precision and recall under imperfect or biased labels, sampling for ground truth, and causal reasoning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the ML lifecycle in production: evaluation, threshold setting, retraining, drift, feature stores and monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have hands-on experience evaluating LLM-based systems, or a strong interest in building rigorous methods for them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are highly proficient in SQL and Python and comfortable working in a modern data stack (e.g. BigQuery, dbt).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can turn messy, cross-system problems into a clear plan, and can explain trade-offs to both technical and non-technical audiences, including senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are fluent in English, both written and spoken.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nice to have: experience in Trust &amp;amp; Safety, fraud prevention, content moderation, or risk management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work perks&amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The opportunity to benefit from our share options programme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days of paid annual leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Newest MacBook models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for you and your family&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frequent team-building events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Home office support: we provide IT workstation equipment and a personal budget of up to €540 for home workplace furniture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lunch benefit per working day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A personal monthly budget for shopping on Vinted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collective Defined Contribution Pension plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NS Business Card for your commute to the office by public transport&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company bike leasing scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly budget for a flexible benefits platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work from Home allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A dog-friendly office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working at Vinted&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workation policy&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Better balance holidays with workdays by working remotely! Up to 90 days per year in the EU, of these, 21 days can be spent globally. For non-EU citizens, it&#39;s 21 days worldwide. This can be combined with time off for vacation or personal time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Individual learning budget&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Each year, you’ll be given a learning budget (starting at €3,000), and a total of up to 10 working days over a 2-year period to support your personal and professional development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hybrid work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our hybrid model, with 2 recommended office days a week, gives you and your team the flexibility to decide if and when you want to work from home, and when to catch up in person.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome applications from everybody, regardless of your background, identity, or life experiences. Job openings come with guides, not checklists. If you’re excited about a role, but don’t identify with every point in the ‘About you’ section, apply anyway – you might still be the perfect match!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The annual gross salary range for this position excluding 8% holiday pay is:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€107.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€144.800 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a> Data Science & Analytics  Amsterdam

Senior Director, Head of Quality & Responsible Person, International  &lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Mavericks Wanted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;When was the last time you achieved the impossible? If that thought feels overwhelming, you might want to pause here, but if it sparks excitement...read on&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;In 2015, we pioneered a “moneyball for biotech” approach, pooling projects and promising early-stage research from academia together under one financial umbrella to reduce risk and unleash innovation. This model allows science and small teams of experts to lead the way. We build bridges to groundbreaking advancements in rare&amp;nbsp;disease, and&amp;nbsp;develop life-changing medicines for patients with unmet needs as fast as humanly possible. &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Together we define white space, push boundaries, and empower people to solve problems. If you&#39;re someone who defies convention, join us and work alongside some of the most respected minds in the industry. Together, we&#39;ll&amp;nbsp;ask&amp;nbsp;&quot;why not?&quot; and help reengineer the future of biopharma. At BridgeBio, we value curiosity and experimentation—including the ethical &amp;amp; thoughtful use of AI to improve clarity, speed, and quality of work.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Sr Director, Head of Quality &amp;amp; Responsible Person, International, leads quality for infigratinib, and will be the designated Responsible Person on the entity&#39;s wholesale distribution authorisation. The role reports to the Head of Quality, QED, with a dotted line to local managing director, and is based in the Netherlands. If the entity becomes the marketing authorisation holder for infigratinib, the role also covers the related MAH quality duties. The role holds an unrestricted right of escalation to the entity&#39;s full board and is independent of commercial operations and of manufacturing/supply with EU-GDP guidelines, relevant EU directives (including the Falsified Medicines Directive), Dutch Medicines Act, and public service requirements. This role acts as a QA liaison of BridgeBio&#39;s contract service providers (CSPs), providing oversight of lot release activities. This role includes reviewing and approving batch records, certificates of analysis, and compliance documents, providing quality review of deviations, change controls, and CAPAs related to assigned CSPs, collaborating closely with CSPs and internal teams such as quality control, manufacturing, regulatory affairs, and supply chain. The role builds and leads a small quality team (deputy RP, QA compliance/QMS, QA operations/GDP), owns the quality management system across the Skeletal Dysplasia assets, and leads WDA licensing, inspection readiness and potentially subsequent MIA readiness, if needed in the future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Major Responsibilities / Accountabilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the named Responsible Person on the WDA: release for distribution, recall decisions, and GDP compliance of the entity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leads and develops the entity&#39;s quality team: deputy RP, QA compliance/QMS, and QA operations/GDP; and QP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manages and improves the Quality Management System (QMS) across the entity&#39;s assets in alignment with the established QMS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the WDA application and IGJ inspection readiness; prepare subsequent MIA readiness (QP recruitment, import and batch-certification processes)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the quality agreement matrix: includes Quality oversight of contract service providers, 3PLs, distributors and intercompany interfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a Quality liaison and provide oversight and quality support of assigned contract service providers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform quality review of assigned quality events such as deviations, change controls, supplier notifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review master manufacturing batch records, including related documents such as specifications, analytical and microbiological methods, stability study protocols, and label proofs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage lot release activities and communication of lot release schedules to key stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate manufacturing deficiencies/non-conformances to management and work with CSPs to ensure timely resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review process and method validation protocols and reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review analytical test results to ensure compliance with approved specifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in updating CMC sections of regulatory and quality documents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in internal and external project team meetings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Other QA/Responsible Person related responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure accuracy of quality of records per GDP requirements including GDPs are implemented and maintained in the quality management system requirements for WDA license&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and coordinate return, rejected, falsified products, recall operations of medicinal products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide oversight of GDP and GMP activities of active pharmaceutical ingredients (API)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure WDA and API registration is current with commercial supply chain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate and leads EU/ROW regulatory inspections&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate and oversee GMP vendor qualification program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the EU/ROW internal audit program, internal training program and ensure data integrity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and review governing procedures as needed (e.g., SOPs, WIs, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Where You’ll Work&amp;nbsp; &lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a Netherlands based remote role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel 30% of time is expected&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Who you are&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS/MS degree preferably in operations, science, pharmacy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A diploma, certificate, or other evidence of formal qualifications on completion of GDP/GDP-API training required for registration as an RP by the competent authorities in the Netherlands&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in pharmaceutical quality, including significant GDP / distribution quality experience; prior appointment as (or eligibility to be) a Responsible Person strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading regulatory inspections with EU competent authorities (IGJ preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience of managing third party vendors (CMOs, CTLs, 3PLs, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior relevant knowledge and experience related to the distribution of medical products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of supply chain concepts, supplier management, inventory management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive knowledge of US/EU GMPs /GDPs and associated guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working in a highly regulated environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven leadership of quality teams; experience building quality functions or systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding the EU and particularly IGJ regulations in relation to the wholesale distribution of medicines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong planning and time management skills with ability to prioritize workload&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills, with keen attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in document and presentation office tools (Microsoft Office, Google Docs, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic understanding of data concepts and enterprise resource planning (ERP) systems e.g., SAP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ready to embrace company core values and diverse corporate culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Rewarding Those Who Make the Mission Possible&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have high expectations for our team members. We make sure those working hard for patients are rewarded and cared for in return.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market leading compensation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid work model - we value your flexibility in how you work, but encourage time in the office to strengthen our culture, collaboration, and sense of community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We provide career development through regular feedback, continuous education and professional development programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We celebrate strong performance with financial rewards, peer-to-peer recognition, and growth opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a global company, our comprehensive benefits may vary based on location.&amp;nbsp; &lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We have high expectations for our team members. We make sure those working hard for patients are rewarded and cared for in return.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
